{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>You shall not turn to.</b> Even in the heart, to gaze." "<b>The elilim.</b> They are the pesilim [carved images], and they are called thus because they are a thing of falsehood, like \"all of you are healers of elil [nothingness]\" (Job 13:4). And it is possible that it is from the root el, and the meaning is that it is nothing." "<b>And gods of casting.</b> Opposite the power of the supernal beings, for there is no need for another god with me; therefore it is written, \"I am YHWH your Elohim.\" And in plural language: \"you shall turn\" and \"you shall make,\" for one who sees and does not report the matter is a partner with him."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:10:53.175441318Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}